{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.no_SL2Z_realizes_trB_q0_proxy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.no_SL2Z_realizes_trB_q0_proxy","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L137-L142","doc":"The prune instantiated at the 6-digit rational proxy `q = 110998/100000` of the\ndocumented substrate q₀ ≈ 1.10998 (`trB` there ≈ 2.6423867 ∈ (2, 3)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.no_SL2Z_realizes_trB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.no_SL2Z_realizes_trB","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**The prune (interval form).** For every `q ∈ [1, 6/5]` — in particular at any\ndocumented q₀ pin — no `M ∈ SL₂(ℤ)` has trace `trB q`; equivalently, no integral\nmonodromy has char-poly `x² − (trB q)·x + 1`. The 2026-06-24 \"M ∈ SL₂(ℤ)\" framing is\nstructurally excluded; the surviving object is a real-analytic SL₂(ℝ) transfer-matrix\nfamily. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trB_not_intCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trB_not_intCast","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L116-L125","doc":"On the whole q₀-bracketing interval, `trB q` is strictly between the consecutive\nintegers 2 and 3, hence not an integer. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trB_lt_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trB_lt_three","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L105-L114","doc":"Upper bound: `trB q < 3` for `q ∈ [1, 6/5]`. The interval `[1, 6/5]` contains\nevery documented substrate pin (q₀ ≈ 1.10998, muon- or proton-anchored). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.two_lt_trB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.two_lt_trB","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L96-L103","doc":"Lower bound: `2 < trB q` for `1 ≤ q`. (In fact `9q⁴ − 8q³ + 8q² − 8q + 9 =\n4(q² − q)² + 5q⁴ + 4(q − 1)² + 5 > 0` for all `q`; positivity of the denominator is\nthe only use of `1 ≤ q`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trB","kind":"def","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L90-L94","doc":"The lever-1 closed-form trace target\n`trB q = 3(3q⁴ + 8q² + 3) / (4q(q+1)²)` (audit\n`2026-06-24-lever1-trB-geometric-target.md`; ≈ 2.6423863 at q₀). Stated over ℚ\n(§7c: no archimedean construct is involved in the obstruction). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.not_exists_SL2Z_trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.not_exists_SL2Z_trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L81-L88","doc":"The gate specialized to `SL₂(ℤ)` (the audit's stated class: monodromies preserving\nthe polarization on `H¹(E)`, char-poly `x² − (tr M)x + 1`). The determinant condition\nis never needed — integrality alone excludes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.not_exists_intMatrix_trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.not_exists_intMatrix_trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L72-L79","doc":"**The reusable integer-trace gate.** If `t : ℚ` is not (the cast of) an integer,\nthen no integer 2×2 matrix has trace `t`. Trivial contrapositive of integrality — but\nthis is exactly the statement that prunes \"find `M` over ℤ with char-poly\n`x² − t·x + 1`\" searches for non-integer `t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trace_intMatrix_eq_intCast","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.TrBIntegerTracePrune.trace_intMatrix_eq_intCast","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/TrBIntegerTracePrune.lean#L65-L70","doc":"The trace of the ℚ-cast of an integer 2×2 matrix is the cast of its (integer)\ntrace. This is the cast form of \"an integer matrix has integer trace\" — the invariant\nbacking the scope-(b) exclusion. ","signatureChunk":0}]}